  "user_request": "For my research project, I'm investigating how neural networks can help identify mutations associated with inherited diseases. I need to understand the scientific approaches used in this area and what has been published about their applications.",
  "response": "The PubMed search returned one record, but it does not directly address neural networks for identifying mutations in inherited diseases. It is a 2016 human-genomics meeting abstract collection; its listed abstract on computational pathogenicity prediction concerns activating variants in oncogenes versus loss-of-function mutations in tumor-suppressor genes, rather than inherited disease or neural networks. This search result therefore provides limited evidence for your project.\n\n- **Human genome meeting 2016 : Houston, TX, USA. 28 February - 2 March 2016.** The record is a meeting abstract collection. Among its abstracts is one on computational algorithms for predicting pathogenicity of cancer-associated variants; the record does not describe a neural-network approach for inherited-disease mutation identification. **Reference:** PubMed, PMID: 27294413 — https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27294413/"
}

