{
  "status": "success",
  "user_request": "For my research project, I'm investigating how neural networks can help identify mutations associated with inherited diseases. I need to understand the scientific approaches used in this area and what has been published about their applications.",
  "response": "The PubMed search returned a deep-learning study of cancer mutations, rather than a study specifically focused on identifying inherited-disease mutations. It offers an example of how neural networks can represent and assess mutation effects, but its reported applications are cancer-related.\n\n1. **“A new deep learning technique reveals the exclusive functional contributions of individual cancer mutations.”** The study describes Continuous Representation of Codon Switches (CRCS), which creates numerical vector representations of mutations. The authors report applying it to detect cancer-related somatic mutations, explore potential driver genes, and score individual tumor mutations; mutation scores were predictive of patient survival in several cancer types. The abstract does not report an application to inherited-disease variant identification. **Source:** PubMed, PMID 35753349 — https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35753349/"
}

{
  "status": "success",
  "user_request": "For my research project, I'm investigating how neural networks can help identify mutations associated with inherited diseases. I need to understand the scientific approaches used in this area and what has been published about their applications.",
  "response": "The PubMed search returned a paper on deep learning for cancer mutations, rather than a study focused specifically on identifying mutations that cause inherited diseases. It describes one computational approach and its reported applications:\n\n- **A new deep learning technique reveals the exclusive functional contributions of individual cancer mutations** (Prashant Gupta et al., 2022). The authors introduce Continuous Representation of Codon Switches (CRCS), which represents mutations as numerical vectors for machine-learning analyses. They report using it to detect cancer-related somatic mutations, explore potential driver genes, and score individual tumor mutations; mutation scores were reported as predictive of patient survival in several cancer types. This paper provides an example of a neural-network approach to mutation analysis, but its applications are cancer-focused, not direct evidence about inherited-disease variant identification. **Source: PubMed, PMID 35753349:** https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35753349/"
}

