  "response": "The PubMed search returned a broad human-genomics conference proceedings record, rather than a study specifically about neural networks for identifying inherited-disease mutations. It does document related research directions, including computational prediction of variant pathogenicity and solving cases using whole-exome sequencing, but the retrieved information does not establish that neural networks were used in those applications.\n\n- **Human genome meeting 2016: Houston, TX, USA. 28 February–2 March 2016.** The proceedings include an abstract on computational algorithms for predicting the pathogenicity of activating variants in oncogenes versus loss-of-function mutations in tumor suppressor genes, and another on solving unsolved whole-exome sequencing cases. These are related to variant interpretation and genetic-disease analysis, but the record does not identify neural networks as the approach. **Source:** PubMed, PMID 27294413 — https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27294413/"
