{
  "status": "success",
  "user_request": "For my research project, I'm investigating how neural networks can help identify mutations associated with inherited diseases. I need to understand the scientific approaches used in this area and what has been published about their applications.",
  "response": "The PubMed result returned here is a broad conference-proceedings record, not a focused study of neural networks for identifying inherited-disease mutations. It therefore does not provide enough evidence to summarize specific neural-network approaches or their applications in that area.\n\n- **Human genome meeting 2016: Houston, TX, USA. 28 February–2 March 2016.** This proceedings record includes diverse genomics presentations. Its abstract mentions a Bayesian classification of biomedical images using features from deep neural networks in a lung-cancer application, as well as separate presentations on Mendelian genomics and variant analysis; it does not establish a neural-network application to inherited-disease mutation identification. **Source:** PubMed, PMID 27294413 — https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27294413/"
